<node id="experiment:P013-1"><data key="type">Experiment</data><data key="label">AutoSkill · Simulation</data><data key="props">{"workId": "work:lin_autoskill_2025", "evidenceId": "P013-1", "sourceId": "P013", "sourceUrl": "https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/10924760", "locator": "Section III.C, equations 2–6, Algorithm 1; Section IV.A–IV.B, Figure 5.", "reviewedAt": "2026-11-24", "reviewStatus": "Fresh targeted primary method/initialization check on 24 November; existing results and evaluation audit reused", "teacher": "fm", "providers": ["fm"], "decision": "include", "scopeLabel": "New-policy RL", "setting": "Simulation", "settingGroup": "Simulation", "task": "Two long-horizon kitchen tasks, Hammer Cleanup, and Stack Three; acquisition of missing skills for completing these tasks.", "taskFamily": "Object manipulation / skill composition", "platform": "Franka Panda in FrankaKitchen and robosuite/MuJoCo", "feedbackSource": "Gemini Pro Vision for binary success; ResNet-50/DistilBERT event-score model pretrained on Ego4D and fine-tuned for tabletop manipulation. Gemini Pro separately proposes skill chains.", "feedback": "Binary success plus scalar event/progress score; the scalar is an MLP score, not cosine similarity.", "levels": ["Rating"], "channel": "", "model": "Gemini Pro Vision for binary success; ResNet-50/DistilBERT event-score model pretrained on Ego4D and fine-tuned for tabletop manipulation. Gemini Pro separately proposes skill chains.", "algorithm": "Modified SAC for modular primitive-parameter policies.", "objective": "After each primitive execution, weighted event and success scores become rewards in replay. Modified SAC optimizes the parameter policies for newly proposed skills and their critics. The LLM planner proposes skills and sketches but the reward module supplies the learning signal.", "policyInitialization": "III.A/III.C.3 and Algorithm 1 learn missing primitive-parameter skill policies from scratch using SAC; IV.A.3 specifies separate MLP actors, while base skills and control primitives are available.", "integration": "After each primitive execution, weighted event and success scores become rewards in replay. Modified SAC optimizes the parameter policies for newly proposed skills and their critics. The LLM planner proposes skills and sketches but the reward module supplies the learning signal.", "comparison": "Sketch RL, CeSD, FIST-ft, and modified SayCan+CLIP, plus reward-component ablations.", "result": "Reported higher task success and oracle-normalized returns than the compared methods in four simulated tasks.", "finding": "Learns missing skill parameters; supplied primitives and skills remain.", "evaluation": "Learning curves across five seeds with standard deviations.", "participants": "", "extraSupport": "Existing base skills and primitive controllers; low-dimensional task and proprioceptive states; pretrained video-language data and tabletop adaptation for the event model. No added ground-truth task reward in the audited missing-skill learning stage.", "limitations": "A supplied skill library, predefined primitive structure and a single missing skill constrain the setup. It is not end-to-end acquisition of every low-level behaviour from an unstructured task instruction.", "scopeReason": "New primitive-parameter skill policies are trained with SAC when a needed skill is absent. Reused base skills and primitive controllers are explicitly retained; this is skill acquisition, not refinement of a pretrained whole-task actor.", "uncertainties": ["The IEEE webpage required JavaScript, so substantive verification used the supplied final journal PDF. Exact primitive-controller transfer implementation is less fully specified than the simulation RL method; do not infer additional on-hardware adaptation."]}</data></node>
