<node id="experiment:P085-1"><data key="type">Experiment</data><data key="label">T2-VLM · Simulation</data><data key="props">{"workId": "work:zhao_training-free_2025", "evidenceId": "P085-1", "sourceId": "P085", "sourceUrl": "https://arxiv.org/html/2507.04789v1", "locator": "Section 4.1 and Figure 5; Appendix A; Appendix C.1–C.2.", "reviewedAt": "2026-11-24", "reviewStatus": "Fresh targeted primary method/initialization check on 24 November; existing results and evaluation audit reused", "teacher": "fm", "providers": ["fm"], "decision": "include", "scopeLabel": "New-policy RL", "setting": "Simulation", "settingGroup": "Simulation", "task": "Place same-colour objects, stack a tower, arrange blocks in a line, and clean up a desk; additional recovery tests.", "taskFamily": "Object manipulation / skill selection", "platform": "Simulated arms in CLIPort and CALVIN", "feedbackSource": "Qwen2-VL as the default evaluator; SAM2 tracking and Bayesian particle filters maintain progress estimates.", "feedback": "Initial binary subgoal-completion judgments converted through tracking into continuous progress-difference rewards.", "levels": ["Rating"], "channel": "", "model": "Qwen2-VL as the default evaluator; SAM2 tracking and Bayesian particle filters maintain progress estimates.", "algorithm": "SAC with an object-centric transformer architecture; temperature set to zero in the appendix.", "objective": "The VLM decomposes the task and initializes subgoal statuses before an episode. Tracking updates progress during execution; progress differences reward SAC updates. The VLM need not be queried at every action for its judgments to influence policy training.", "policyInitialization": "Appendix A jointly updates CNN/self-attention/policy/value networks under SAC. Appendix C.2 defines object/skill-combination actions implemented by primitive controllers, with no loaded task actor described.", "integration": "The VLM decomposes the task and initializes subgoal statuses before an episode. Tracking updates progress during execution; progress differences reward SAC updates. The VLM need not be queried at every action for its judgments to influence policy training.", "comparison": "Environment rewards, VLM-CaR and RL-VLM-F for learning; planning baselines for recovery.", "result": "Reported subgoal-completion curves are comparable to environment rewards and stronger than VLM-CaR and RL-VLM-F in the tested setup. Recovery experiments measure task success and number of high-level actions.", "finding": "Learns choices over supplied skills; hardware branch only tests rewards.", "evaluation": "Three seeds; 400 training episodes on CLIPort tasks and 2,000 on CALVIN; recovery evaluated over 20 trials.", "participants": "", "extraSupport": "Task text and execution primitives. Simulator-provided object boxes are used by the policy; reward computation uses SAM2 rather than those privileged boxes.", "limitations": "Simulation only for policy learning. The learned action selects picking/placing objects or combinations of named skills and objects; do not describe this as necessarily learning low-level motor control. Subgoal-completion ratio is not identical to full-task success.", "scopeReason": "New SAC task-level object/skill selection learns from VLM-initialized tracked rewards. Count high-level task-policy learning, with existing primitives explicit; do not describe motor control learned from scratch.", "uncertainties": ["Physical task names are not fully specified in the passages retained for this targeted review; do not invent them. No hardware policy update is evidenced in the inspected methods and experiments."]}</data></node>
